# Benchmark runs are large and mostly regenerable, so the tree is ignored -- EXCEPT the
# kernel transcripts, which are the only published evidence for the axiom-footprint claims.
# Ignoring those made every "verified declarations" count in the README a self-report, which
# is exactly what this project refuses to accept from anyone else. 88 KB is a cheap price for
# a claim that a reader can check without cloning anything.
benchmark_runs/*
!benchmark_runs/v5.6.1/
benchmark_runs/v5.6.1/*
!benchmark_runs/v5.6.1/logs/
!benchmark_runs/v5.7.0/
benchmark_runs/v5.7.0/*
!benchmark_runs/v5.7.0/logs/
# The global `*.log` rule above also catches these, so it has to be overridden explicitly.
# These last two lines are what actually publishes the evidence; without them the six lines
# above look correct and do nothing, which is the failure mode this programme keeps finding.
!benchmark_runs/v5.6.1/logs/*.log
!benchmark_runs/v5.7.0/logs/*.log

# LaTeX build byproducts
*.bbl
*.blg
